## enterprise-linux audit baseline -- base configuration (layer 13)
## Implementation guide (CIS/STIG-oriented via ComplianceAsCode), not a
## certification claim. Loaded by augenrules, which concatenates rules.d/*.rules
## in lexical order and hoists -D to the top and the last -e to the end.
##
## Key naming: every rule carries "-k el_<area>" so a SIEM can filter on the
## "key" field. Keys are listed in security/hardening/README.md.

## Remove any existing rules
-D

## Kernel backlog; laptops with bursty activity need more than the default 64.
-b 8192
--backlog_wait_time 60000

## Failure mode: 1 = printk. 2 (panic) is a STIG option but unacceptable on
## end-user laptops.
-f 1

## Ignore errors while loading (e.g. watches on paths that do not exist on
## this distro family, such as /etc/apparmor.d on RHEL).
-i
